Authoritative cumulative snapshot of ref/linux-7.1.5 with the cooperative
ethernet device, R1: the device registers and nothing more runs.

Generated against download/linux-7.1.5.tar.xz on 2026-08-01.

Over the shutdown snapshot:

  * drivers/net/conet_colinux.c -- a cooperative ethernet netdev on the
    console's transport, one size up: co_colinux_net_io holds a TX and an RX
    byte ring in ordinary kernel .bss (128 KB each), one writer per word per
    direction, frames carried whole as a 32-bit length plus payload padded to
    a four-byte boundary. Records start four-byte aligned so the length word
    never straddles the wrap. The host will reach the rings the way it reaches
    the console's, by resolving the symbol and walking the guest's page
    tables; the struct layout is ABI and is documented in the file.

    TX copies the skb into the ring and yields, exactly the trade put_chars
    makes; a full ring drops the frame rather than stopping the queue,
    because a stopped queue wedges every writer against a host that may never
    drain. RX is a polling kthread, started at ndo_open, feeding netif_rx; a
    ring desync is reported and resynchronised empty rather than parsed.

    In this snapshot the interface is registered and DOWN: the TX path, RX
    kthread and rings are compiled in and inert until something opens the
    device. Self-gated on co_colinux_guest, obj-y like cobd, no Kconfig
    symbol to forget.

This file is intentionally not listed in series: it preserves the exact live
guest source while the incremental patch set is still being repaired.

